// Disk images written by `hdiutil create -srcfolder` on macOS, so the reader
// is checked against what Apple's own tools produce rather than against images
// built by the same understanding of the format it reads them with.
//
// The HFS+ and APFS images hold one tree, `Fixture`: a text file, an empty one,
// an executable script, a nested folder, a hard link pair, a link inside the
// image and an installer shortcut to /Applications, a Hangul name and one with
// a colon. `hfs-ulfo` adds `big.bin`, 1.25 MB of a repeated 3,000-byte block,
// which spans several image chunks. Each image uses a different chunk codec
// (ULFO = LZFSE, ULMO = LZMA, UDBZ = bzip2, UDZO = zlib) or partition layout
// (`hfs-apm` = Apple partition map, `hfs-none` = no partition map at all).
//
// The FAT images hold `HELLO.TXT`, a long file name and a subfolder. The
// `decmpfs` images hold files macOS stored with filesystem compression
// (`ditto --hfsCompression`): `attr.txt` small enough to sit in its attribute
// and `fork.txt` cut into 64 KiB chunks in its resource fork, both LZVN.

